// Slur, tie and glissando in the SECOND voice of a single-staff polyphony
// (voice { } voice { }). The detectors used to scan only the primary voice, so
// voice 2's spanners vanished entirely. They now run per voice and lay out
// against voice 2's own note columns (its stem-down slur curves UP, its tie and
// glissando attach to voice-2 heads). Voice 1 carries no spanners, so any curve
// here belongs to voice 2. LILYPOND-REF: ly/engraver-init.ly — Slur/Tie/
// Glissando engravers run in each Voice context.
octave absolute
title "Multi-voice spanners"
part mel { clef treble }
section S {
  mel {
    voice { c''4 d'' e'' f'' | g''4 a'' b'' c''' | }
    voice { e'4@glissando g' g'( e') | f'4 f'~ f' f' | }
  }
}
form main { S }
score main "multivoice-spanners" { staff mel }
